        "object": "<p>Berlin expected to outline response to incident this month widely speculated to have been coordinated by Russia</p><p>The German government is imminently expected to announce who it believes was behind a suspected <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/06/leipzig-drone-bomb-found-near-ukrainian-plane-carrying-ammunition\">drone attack on a Ukrainian cargo plane</a> earlier this month and to outline its response to the incident in coordination with its European and Nato partners.</p><p>The chancellor, Friedrich Merz, told the public broadcaster ARD in an interview on Sunday evening: “We are in the process of concluding the investigations; we have reached a broad agreement within the federal government on how we will respond, and we will make this clear in the coming days. It won’t take much longer.”</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/31/germany-leipzig-drone-attack-ukrainian-plane\">Continue reading...</a>"
